# Neo Spectral parameters (docs/specs/mastering-tools.md §5.16). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoSpectral
namespace NeoBuzz.Spectral
class NeoSpectralMachine
summary Dynamic resonance suppressor working on a short-time spectrum (2048-point frames, hop a quarter of that): each frequency is compared with a reference, and where it stands out the machine turns that narrow region down for as long as it does, so harsh ringing, boxiness and sibilant peaks are smoothed without a fixed EQ. Suppress compares each bin with the spectrum around it, Balance moves the whole spectrum toward a pink slope (with a tilt), Stabilize pulls the short-term spectrum toward its own long-term average. Depth, Knee, Selectivity and Smoothing shape what counts as a resonance; Lift lets it also fill dips. Region keeps it to a frequency range, Mix and Delta (hear only what it takes out) check it. The latency is the frame (43 ms at 44.1 and 48 kHz, reported). Use it on a vocal, a guitar, a mix bus or a master for harshness and resonances that move.

group Detector
Mode       "Mode"           0 2     0     enum Suppress Balance Stabilize | Suppress: each bin against the spectrum around it. Balance: the whole spectrum against a pink slope plus Tilt. Stabilize: the short-term spectrum against its own long-term average (4 s)
    how Chooses what the spectrum is compared with: its neighbourhood (Suppress), a pink slope (Balance) or its own long-term average (Stabilize).
    sound Suppress calms narrow, ringing peaks; Balance evens out an overall tonal tilt; Stabilize keeps a part of the spectrum from jumping out from moment to moment.
Depth      "Depth"          0 1000  500   pct                                 | How much of what stands out is taken out: 100 % brings it to the reference
    how Sets how much of the excess over the reference is removed, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Low values tame resonances gently; 100 % removes them completely and can sound hollow.
Knee       "Knee"           0 1000  333   lin 1 10 dB 1                       | How far over the reference a bin must stand before it is acted on (softly: little below, nearly full above)
    how Sets how far a frequency must stand out before the machine reacts, from 1 to 10 dB.
    sound A low knee also touches ordinary variation and can dull the sound; a high one only catches clear resonances.
Selectivity "Selectivity"   0 1000  333   lin 0.1 1 oct 2                     | Half-width of the neighbourhood a bin is compared with, in octaves (Suppress, and the smoothing of Balance)
    how Sets how wide the reference neighbourhood is, from 0.1 to 1 octave.
    sound Narrow values catch only needle-thin peaks; wide ones also catch broad bumps in the tone.
Smoothing  "Smoothing"      0 6     2     int 0                                                   | Widens the cut across neighbouring frequencies (each bin is 23 Hz at 48 kHz)
    how Spreads each cut over neighbouring frequency bins, from 0 to 6.
    sound Larger values make the cuts broader and softer; 0 gives the narrowest, most surgical notches.
Tilt       "Tilt"           0 1000  500   lin -6 6 dB/oct 1                   | Balance only: slope added to the pink target above 300 Hz
    how Tilts the Balance target above 300 Hz, from -6 to +6 dB per octave.
    sound Positive values aim for a brighter balance, negative for a darker one.
Lift       "Lift"           0 1000  0     lin 0 12 dB 1                       | How much a dip below the reference may be filled in (0: cut only)
    how Sets how far the machine may raise frequencies that sit below the reference, from 0 to 12 dB.
    sound At 0 it only cuts; a few dB fill holes and even out the tone but can also lift noise.
group Time
Attack     "Attack"         0 1000  500   time 0.002 0.2                      | How fast a cut comes in (faster at high frequencies)
    how Sets how fast a cut comes in, from 2 ms to 200 ms (faster in the highs).
    sound Short attacks catch a resonance as it starts; long ones leave the start of each note untouched.
Release    "Release"        0 1000  437   time 0.02 2                         | How fast a cut lets go (faster at high frequencies)
    how Sets how fast a cut lets go, from 20 ms to 2 s (faster in the highs).
    sound Short releases follow the signal closely; long ones are smoother and more stable.
group Region
Low        "Low limit"      0 1000  199   freq 40 4000                        | Below this frequency nothing is changed
    how Sets the lowest frequency the machine works on, from 40 Hz to 4 kHz.
    sound Raise it to keep the bass and the body of the sound untouched.
High       "High limit"     0 1000  903   freq 2000 20000                     | Above this frequency nothing is changed
    how Sets the highest frequency the machine works on, from 2 kHz to 20 kHz.
    sound Lower it to keep the air and the top end untouched.
group Output
Mix        "Mix"            0 1000  1000  pct                                 | Wet against dry; at 0 % the output is the delayed input, bit for bit
    how Blends the processed signal with the dry one (delayed to match).
    sound Parallel use keeps the character of the source while the suppression still smooths it.
Output     "Output"         0 480   240   db -24 24                           | Gain after the suppressor, 0.1 dB steps (the editor's Match sets it from the gain-match reading)
    how Adds -24 to +24 dB of gain after the suppressor.
    sound It matches the loudness to the untreated signal so you can judge the tone fairly.
Delta      "Delta"          0 1     0     switch                              | Hear only what the suppressor takes out: the output minus the input, delayed to match (glides over 10 ms)
    how Plays only the difference between the output and the input.
    sound You hear exactly what is being removed, so you can check it is resonance and not the body of the sound.

# What the suppressor measures (NeoSpectralMachine.Readings, machine_readings).
reading reduction_db      dB    | The deepest cut now, dB (0 or more)
reading mean_reduction_db dB    | The mean cut over the working region now, dB (0 or more)
reading gain_match_db     dB    | Short-term loudness out − in (K-weighted, 3 s)
reading latency_samples   samples | The frame, N − 1 (2047 at 44.1 and 48 kHz), reported to NeoBuzz Live
